    "younger_18_44": "Ages 18-44: Age is generally not a significant factor.",
    "younger_45_49": "Ages 45-49: Age begins to be a factor, especially with limited education and unskilled work history.",
    "approaching_advanced_50_54": "Ages 50-54: Age significantly limits the types of work an individual can adjust to.",
    "advanced_55_59": "Ages 55-59: The SSA considers the vocational adversity of age much more seriously. Many directed decisions favor the claimant.",
    "close_to_retirement_60_plus": "Ages 60+: Very favorable. Most claimants with even moderate limitations are approved."
  },
